1
00:00:03,060 --> 00:00:08,140
War and Peace is a famously long book spanning around 1,400 pages

2
00:00:08,619 --> 00:00:10,199
with 559 characters.

3
00:00:11,339 --> 00:00:14,300
Written by Leo Tolstoy in the mid-19th century,

4
00:00:14,640 --> 00:00:21,559
it began as a short novel about a failed revolutionary in the unsuccessful Decemberist Revolt of 1825.

5
00:00:22,839 --> 00:00:26,339
But as Tolstoy wrote the book, the story kept on expanding

6
00:00:26,920 --> 00:00:28,019
and expanding.

7
00:00:28,620 --> 00:00:35,020
What started as a book about one member of a group trying and failing to overthrow the autocratic rule of

8
00:00:35,060 --> 00:00:37,100
the Tsar turned into something much bigger.

9
00:00:38,100 --> 00:00:40,659
The Decemberist Revolt proved too small a subject,

10
00:00:41,420 --> 00:00:45,460
so Tolstoy turned to Napoleon's invasion of Russia in 1812.

11
00:00:46,159 --> 00:00:51,939
One protagonist became three, and when his ideas outstripped the narrative limitations of a novel,

12
00:00:52,219 --> 00:00:55,159
he would turn the chapter into a philosophical essay.

13
00:00:56,340 --> 00:00:58,640
The novel took over his entire life.

14
00:00:59,359 --> 00:01:05,599
Family history, autobiography and spiritual preoccupations would weave their way into the story.

